Package: libras3d
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Standalone GRASS raster3d replacement library (runtime)
 ras3d reimplements the GRASS GIS raster3d API as a standalone shared
 library that reads hyperspectral data cubes from multi-band GeoTIFF
 and HDF-EOS5 (HDF5) files.  It provides drop-in replacements for
 GRASS functions (Rast3d_*, G_*, Rast_*) so that i.hyper.* processing
 modules can run outside GRASS without modification.
 .
 Reads are parallelised with OpenMP; output is always GeoTIFF with
 LZW compression and 512x512 tiles.
 .
 This package contains the shared library (libras3d.so).

Package: libras3d-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: libras3d (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends},
 libtiff-dev, libgeotiff-dev, libhdf5-dev
Description: Standalone GRASS raster3d replacement library (development)
 ras3d reimplements the GRASS GIS raster3d API as a standalone shared
 library that reads hyperspectral data cubes from multi-band GeoTIFF
 and HDF-EOS5 (HDF5) files.
 .
 This package contains the C headers, static library, and pkg-config
 file needed to build software against libras3d.

Package: libras3d-python
Architecture: all
Depends: libras3d (>= ${source:Version}), python3, python3-numpy,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Python ctypes wrapper for libras3d
 Provides open_cube(), get_band(), get_region(), and read_all_bands()
 returning NumPy float32 arrays.  Loads libras3d.so at runtime via
 ctypes; no compiled extension is required.
